 ## Scope and Limitations
 
-- **Detection and metadata only.** `ImageProbe` identifies a format and reads its header fields;
-  it never decodes pixel data, so there is no rendering, editing, or format-conversion
-  capability anywhere in the library.
-- **Frame count reflects only what the container itself records.** It is a real, computed count
-  for GIF, ICO, TIFF, and bundled multi-page DJVU (DJVM); every other supported format reports a
-  fixed `1` for a successfully parsed header, since none of their headers carry a genuine frame
-  or page count. An indirect (multi-file) DJVM document, or a truncated bundled one, reports
-  `FrameCount` as `null`, since its pages can't all be seen from the one file.
-- **Non-placeable WMF is detected but not dimensioned.** The classic (non-placeable) WMF header
-  carries no bounding rectangle, so `Probe` returns a format-only `ImageInfo` for it; only the
-  placeable WMF header (identified by its own magic number) yields `Width`/`Height`.
-  Placeable-WMF dimensions assume a conventional 96 DPI target, since the header only stores
-  units-per-inch bounds.
-- **DICOM parsing stops at the first undefined-length element.** A sequence or encapsulated
-  pixel-data element with an undefined length ends the walk rather than being parsed, since
-  `Rows`/`Columns`/`BitsAllocated` always precede such elements in a conformant file.
-- **CDR support is planned but not yet implemented** — no `CdrFormatHandler` exists in the
-  current source tree.
-
-These limitations apply only to Aspose.Imaging FOSS — they don't carry over to
-[Aspose.Imaging for .NET — Enterprise Edition](https://products.aspose.com/imaging/net/), which
-adds full decoding, editing, rendering, and conversion across a much broader format range.
+`Probe` never throws on malformed or truncated input — if a file matches a format's signature but its header can't be fully parsed, you get back an `ImageInfo` with just the `Format` set rather than an exception.
+
+- **Detection and metadata only.** `ImageProbe` identifies a format and reads its header fields; it never decodes pixel data, so there is no rendering, editing, or format-conversion capability anywhere in the library.
+- **Frame count reflects only what the container itself records.** It is a real, computed count for GIF, ICO, TIFF, and bundled multi-page DJVU (DJVM); every other supported format reports a fixed `1` for a successfully parsed header, since none of their headers carry a genuine frame or page count. An indirect (multi-file) DJVM document, or a truncated bundled one, reports `FrameCount` as `null`, since its pages can't all be seen from the one file.
+- **Non-placeable WMF is detected but not dimensioned.** The classic (non-placeable) WMF header carries no bounding rectangle, so `Probe` returns a format-only `ImageInfo` for it; only the placeable WMF header (identified by its own magic number) yields `Width`/`Height`. Placeable-WMF dimensions assume a conventional 96 DPI target, since the header only stores units-per-inch bounds.
+- **DICOM parsing stops at the first undefined-length element.** A sequence or encapsulated pixel-data element with an undefined length ends the walk rather than being parsed, since `Rows`/`Columns`/`BitsAllocated` always precede such elements in a conformant file.
+- **CDR support is planned but not yet implemented** — no `CdrFormatHandler` exists in the current source tree.
+
+See [Aspose.Imaging for .NET — Enterprise Edition](https://products.aspose.com/imaging/net/). It adds full decoding, editing, rendering, and conversion across a much broader format range.
 
